  "result": "Perfect! All 201 tests pass. The credit notes feature is complete.\n\n**Summary of implementation:**\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added error code:\n- `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH`: \"Credit note amount cannot exceed the invoice total.\"\n\n**src/numbering.js** \u2014 Added function:\n- `nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)` \u2014 generates CN-YYYY-NNNN format with separate counter from invoices\n\n**src/credits.js** \u2014 New module with `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` that:\n- Returns NOT_ISSUED for draft invoices\n- Returns AMOUNT_INVALID if amount is not a positive integer\n- Returns DATE_INVALID if date is invalid\n- Returns CREDIT_TOO_HIGH if amount exceeds invoice total (from invoiceTotals)\n- Works on 'issued', 'partially_paid', and 'paid' invoices\n- Returns ok(creditNote) with: `{ number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }`\n- Credit note numbers use separate CN-YYYY-NNNN counter from invoices\n- Properly handles mixed invoice and credit note numbers in existingNumbers\n\n**test/credits.test.js** \u2014 18 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Creation for all allowed statuses (issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- Error handling (NOT_ISSUED, AMOUNT_INVALID, DATE_INVALID, CREDIT_TOO_HIGH)\n- Edge cases (zero, negative, fractional amounts; invalid dates)\n- Counter behavior (increments per year, separate from invoices, padding)\n- Respect for discounts and vouchers on invoices\n- Field preservation and data integrity",
